  "body": "Closes #1174\nClaim: cloud/fb-quickwins-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/fb-quickwins-sonnet)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (cloud/review-1227-opus, round 1: REQUEST CHANGES, fixed in the head; round 2 pending)\n\n### Problem\nThe seasonal arrival alert is informative, shown at app start, with a title (« Oh Oh Oh ! ») that says nothing, and neither button has the cancel role, so Esc / ⌘. on a hardware keyboard has nothing to trigger (HIG › Alerts: a title that describes the situation; avoid alerts that only inform). Legacy has the same class of alert, simpler (`Classes/HFRplusAppDelegate.m:665-676` @ 87fe0d1c, GAP-147).\n\n### Cause\n`SeasonalArrivalAlert` used the greeting as title and plain buttons; its binding setter ignores dismissal, so only a button can answer.\n\n### Change\nThis is the **smallest step** of the issue; the larger one (no alert, a note in Réglages › Thème) remains the operator's call. **The title wording is mine to confirm.**\n- `SeasonalThemeModel.title(for:)` names the situation **from the model's state** (review round 1: the alert is also pending when nothing was switched on, on 25–26/12, with automatic themes off, or after the user picked another theme first): « Thème de Noël activé » when a theme is active, « Thème de Noël » otherwise. `Alert.message` keeps « Thème disponible dans les réglages ».\n- `SeasonalArrivalAlert` uses them and gives « OK » `role: .cancel`, so Esc answers « OK » (keeps whatever is on) through the existing `answer(disable: false)`.\n- Docs that quoted the old title: `docs/THEMES.md` (Noël row, and a note on the Samain row: LOT-191's title must name the situation and be true when nothing is switched on), `docs/lots/LOT-166-seasonal-noel.md`, the mockup note in `docs/assets/themes/tokens/themes.json`, the mockup generator `tooling/illustrations/build.py`; code comments. The Samain alert itself is not implemented (`Alert` has only `noelArrival`); its wording stays for LOT-191.\n\n### Tests\n`SeasonalArrivalAlertTextTests` (model-backed): on 01/12 Noël soft is on and the title is « Thème de Noël activé »; on 25 and 26/12 and with automatic themes off nothing is on and the title is « Thème de Noël » (these fail with the first version's constant); no title greets. The cancel role and Esc are SwiftUI wiring: Mac check on #893 (iPad with a keyboard: Esc dismisses it keeping the theme). Not run here (Linux); `compile-check` runs on the head.\n\n### Ledger\n\n```gap-edit\nGAP-147\nSwiftHFR final: Noël (Noël soft, Noël abusé) selectable 01/12–26/12 on local dates every year, Noël soft switched on 01/12–24/12 unless opted out, arrival: Santa's sleigh pulled by its reindeer crosses the screen, then the « Thème de Noël activé » alert (« Thème de Noël » when nothing was switched on; « OK » the cancel role, #1174); elves packing and restore of the previous theme (silent after 02/01); Noël soft = legacy's red accent over the Legacy theme, a gallery theme keeping its own accent (operator, 2026-11-12), never stored, procedural light snow (legacy's snow frames have no stated licence), snow piled on the first card and in the bottom corners, and a Christmas object crossing the screen every 20–90 min of foreground time; Samain 01/10–31/10 (LOT-191); 14 July overlay (LOT-194); « Thèmes de saison automatiques » and « Animations de saison » settings (docs/THEMES.md §4–§5).\n```\n\n---\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CDvQG8jqNrseTphdnF",
