   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/review-1227-opus, round 1): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 8ca36e6a\n\n1. **High: the new title can be false.** `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/Seasons/SeasonalThemeModel.swift:35` always shows « Thème de Noël activé ». But `arrive(year:switching:)` (`:154-161`) stores the arrival as pending even when nothing gets switched on. The existing tests already pin two such cases, each ending with `activeTheme == nil` and `pendingAlert == .noelArrival(year: 2026)`: `on25And26DecemberTheArrivalPlaysButNothingIsSwitchedOn` (`SeasonalThemeModelTests.swift:40-49`) and `withAutomaticThemesOffTheArrivalSwitchesNothingOn` (`:185-197`). There is a third case: the alert is kept across launches, so a user who picks their own theme first (`select(nil)` → `restore`) still gets « activé ». In all of these the alert says a theme is on when it is off, and « Désactiver » opts out of a theme that was never on. The PR body's « the theme is on when the alert shows » is wrong, and `docs/THEMES.md:86` now contradicts itself in one cell (« activé » on 25–26/12 next to « without switching anything on »). Fix: base the title on the model's state (for example « Thème de Noël activé » only when `activeTheme != nil`, otherwise a title such as « Thème de Noël disponible »), or use a neutral title. Add a model test on 25/12 and with automatic themes off that fails with the current constant.\n2. **Low: the test cannot catch item 1.** `SeasonalArrivalTests.swift:80-86` (`SeasonalArrivalAlertTextTests`) only compares a constant with itself. Test the title together with the model state, as in item 1.\n3. **Low: the same issue remains in the specs.** `tooling/illustrations/build.py:344` still draws the mockup with « Oh Oh Oh ! ». The Samain rows (`docs/THEMES.md:87`, `themes.json:682`, `build.py:347`) still give « Spooktober est là ! » as the title, so LOT-191 will port the same HIG problem. Update the generator, and add a note to the Samain row (or to the LOT-191 issue) saying the title must name the situation (#1174).\n4. **Detail:** the GAP-147 `gap-edit` passes `check-body` and changes only the alert clause; the `,,` after « never stored » was already in the row and can be fixed now. Its wording « the « Thème de Noël activé » alert » is affected by item 1.\n\n**Vérifié:** diff `origin/dev-swift...8ca36e6a`; `ledger.py check-body --pr 1227` on the live body (ok); compared it with the GAP-147 row on dev-swift; `themes.json` is valid JSON and no tooling parses its `then` field; `git grep` for « Oh Oh Oh » and « Spooktober »; SwiftLint on `Settings/Seasons` (app and tests) passes; read the model paths for dismissal and answering: no path dismisses without `answer`, and there is no double answer (guard on `pendingAlert`). Esc on the cancel role is still the Mac check (#893). App tests not run (Linux).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
