   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/review-1227-opus-r2, round 2): APPROVE** — head 0f299b76\n\nRound 1 findings, checked against the code:\n- **(1) High, fixed.** `activeTheme` (SeasonalThemeModel.swift:263) holds a Noël theme only: `SeasonalTheme` has two cases, `noelSoft` and `noelAbuse`, and `onTheme` returns one of them. So `!= nil` is the right test; checking for `.noelSoft || .noelAbuse` would mean the same thing. A gallery theme never clears the Noël overlay (operator decision (a)), so « activé » stays true then. If the user turns Noël off in « Thèmes de saison » before the alert shows, `select(nil)` clears it and the title becomes « Thème de Noël ». Scene activation, or midnight passing from 24 to 25/12, never turns a theme off while the alert waits: `arrivalOnly` does not restore it, and on 27/12 `pendingAlert` becomes nil, which closes the alert.\n- **(2) Low, fixed.** The tests now go through the model. Mutating the code to the old constant title, or to `true` in place of the `activeTheme` check, fails the 25/12, 26/12 and automatic-off tests.\n- **(3) and (4), fixed.** build.py, the Samain row in THEMES.md, LOT-166 and themes.json are updated. The ledger block in the live PR body is word for word the current row, with only the « Oh Oh Oh » clause replaced and the `,,` corrected.\n\nFindings:\n1. **Detail.** SeasonalArrivalAlert.swift:22: the title is recomputed on every body evaluation. On an iPad with two windows, turning Noël off in the second window while the alert is up in the first switches the title to « Thème de Noël ». The new title is still true. No fix needed.\n2. **Detail, outside #1174.** With nothing switched on (25–26/12, automatic themes off), « Désactiver » only opts out of a season in which nothing would be switched on anyway. Worth a follow-up issue for the alert's wording, not this PR.\n\n**Vérifié**\n- The round-2 changes and the full PR diff, read alongside the model and the alert view.\n- `python3 tooling/docs/ledger.py check-body --pr 1227` on the live PR body: 1 block ok. A script check that the new cell equals the current row with only the intended changes: true.\n- SwiftLint on the Seasons sources and tests, in a throwaway worktree: clean. Line 22 is 140 characters, at the limit.\n- A repository-wide search for « Oh Oh Oh »: what is left is in the GAP row (replaced by the ledger) and in history notes.\n- The worktree is removed.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
